{"assets":["/statement-assets/885d0d91f095df5ffcb038c06bc136c1b8cb8362eef6973f9e0f32dc5e0a97bd.png","/statement-assets/6be577636bf60cbffa7db8811dfac83349c68375f8869226bc6429fd21f04c76.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1790","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Timofey and Black-White Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Timofey came to a famous summer school and found a tree on $$$n$$$ vertices. A tree is a connected undirected graph without cycles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Every vertex of this tree, except $$$c_0$$$, is colored "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"white"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The vertex $$$c_0$$$ is colored "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Timofey wants to color all the vertices of this tree in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, he performs $$$n - 1$$$ operations. During the $$$i$$$-th operation, he selects the vertex $$$c_i$$$, which is currently "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"white"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and paints it "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positivity"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of tree the minimum distance between all pairs of different "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices in it. The distance between the vertices $$$v$$$ and $$$u$$$ is the number of edges on the path from $$$v$$$ to $$$u$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After each operation, Timofey wants to know the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positivity"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the current tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains the integers $$$n, c_0$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le c_0 \\le n$$$) — the number of vertices in the tree and index of the initial "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each testcase contains $$$n - 1$$$ unique integers $$$c_1, c_2, \\dots, c_{n-1}$$$ ($$$1 \\le c_i \\le n$$$, $$$c_i \\ne c_0$$$), where $$$c_i$$$ is the vertex which is colored "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" during the $$$i$$$-th operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n - 1$$$ row of each testcase contains the integers $$$v_i, u_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le v_i, u_i \\le n$$$) — edges in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ for all testcases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, print $$$n - 1$$$ integer on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The integer with index $$$i$$$ must be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positivity"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the tree obtained by the first $$$i$$$ operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n6 6\n4 1 3 5 2\n2 4\n6 5\n5 3\n3 4\n1 3\n4 2\n4 1 3\n3 1\n2 3\n1 4\n10 3\n10 7 6 5 2 9 8 1 4\n1 2\n1 3\n4 5\n4 3\n6 4\n8 7\n9 8\n10 8\n1 8\n7 3\n7 5 1 2 4 6\n1 2\n3 2\n4 5\n3 4\n6 5\n7 6\n9 7\n9 3 1 4 2 6 8 5\n4 1\n8 9\n4 8\n2 6\n7 3\n2 4\n3 5\n5 4\n10 2\n1 8 5 10 6 9 4 3 7\n10 7\n7 8\n3 6\n9 7\n7 6\n4 2\n1 6\n7 5\n9 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2 1 1 1 \n3 1 1 \n3 2 2 2 2 2 1 1 1 \n4 2 2 1 1 1 \n5 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 \n4 3 2 2 1 1 1 1 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, after the second operation, the tree looks like this: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/885d0d91f095df5ffcb038c06bc136c1b8cb8362eef6973f9e0f32dc5e0a97bd.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The distance between vertices $$$1$$$ and $$$6$$$ is $$$3$$$, the distance between vertices $$$4$$$ and $$$6$$$ is $$$3$$$, the distance between vertices $$$1$$$ and $$$4$$$ is $$$2$$$. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positivity"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of this tree is equal to the minimum of these distances. It equals $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third testcase, after the fourth operation, the tree looks like this: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6be577636bf60cbffa7db8811dfac83349c68375f8869226bc6429fd21f04c76.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positivity"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of this tree is $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1790F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1790/problem/F"}